# /etc/default/astro-process on the eclipticam Pi.
#
# REFERENCE COPY ONLY — the live file is rendered by ansible from
# roles/eclipticam-astro/templates/astro-process.env.j2, driven by
# `eclipticam_process_cameras` in inventory/host_vars/eclipticam.yml.
# Ansible is authoritative; edit there, not here.
#
# The eclipticam Pi DOES run stage 3 (deliverables), since 2026-08 when it
# gained its own SSD at /mnt/ssd, bind-mounted to ~/eclipticam-frames. That
# was always the stated condition for a Pi to process "self": the old
# objection was reading every frame back over NFS on a weak CPU (~13x slower
# than puppy reading locally; astrocam backfill 2026-06-20). With the frames
# LOCAL that objection is gone, and storage locality now favours the Pi.
#
# eclipticam therefore owns eclipticam-v1 + eclipticam-v3w end to end:
# stage 1 (astro-state), capture, and stage 3 (astro-process). Nothing on
# puppy or muppet should name these cameras — the dispatcher requires
# exactly one host's CAMERAS list per camera (see bin/astro-process).
CAMERAS="--camera eclipticam-v1 --camera eclipticam-v3w"
